    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d282">

                <pb facs="0362" n="288" sameAs="frus:frus1918Russiav01/pg288"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 861.00/775</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Sweden</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Morris</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram—Extract]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Stockholm</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-12-06T14:00:00+01:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">December 6, 1917, 2 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received December 7, 6.15
                        a.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1126. Referring to following reported interview which appeared in the Swedish
                    newspapers and is supposed to have taken place between General Judson, the American military attaché
                    (no doubt the newspapers in error gave the name of Jackson
                    instead of Judson), <pb facs="0363"
                        n="289" xml:id="pg289"/> and Trotsky
                    and which was contained in my telegram No. 1106.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d282-f1"/>
                    This has been causing a great deal of comment in Sweden. In an informal
                    conversation with the Foreign Minister yesterday on other matters he asked me as
                    to the authenticity of this report regarding statement of Judson’s. I quote below <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Dagens Nyheter</hi> report regarding interview. …</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Morris</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
